 75AS c  See also DDEP evaluations (2010BeZQ, 1999BeZS) for decay of {+75}Se;   
 75AS2c  also on DDEP webpage: www.nucleide.org/DDEP.htm. In the opinion of     
 75AS3c  evaluators, the gamma-ray intensities and branching ratios given       
 75AS4c  in the DDEP evaluation for the 821.8-keV level are incorrect. The      
 75AS5c  DDEP evaluators took these data mainly from 2005Ra29.                  
 75AS c  Although 2005Ra29 is the most recent experiment, but due to many       
 75AS2c  inconsistencies in this paper, the results are not used much in        
 75AS3c  this evaluation. The authors also report ce measurements and give      
 75AS4c  K-shell (also M- and N-shell in some cases) conversion coefficients,   
 75AS5c  some of which are quoted to a precision of 1% or less, which does not  
 75AS6c  seem realistic. No |g|g coincidence study was done in this work.       
 75AS7c  The 859.84, 1/2+ and 586.81, 1/2- levels reported to be populated in   
 75AS8c  this decay by 2005Ra29 only are omitted here since none of the |g rays 
 75AS9c  associated with these levels have been seen in other studies. In       
 75ASAc  addition, the 859.84 level is within 5 keV of the Q value and implied  
 75ASBc  log| {Ift}=3.2 is impossible for a 5/2+ to 1/2+ |b transition.         
 75ASCc  Branching ratios of |g transitions reported in 2005Ra29 are in         
 75ASDc  severe disagreement with those from (n,n'|g) study where this          
 75ASEc  level is strongly populated                                            
