 75AS cG E(A)$From 2000He14, based on a revised energy scale that uses the new  
 75AS2cG fundamental constants and wave lengths from an updated value of the    
 75AS3cG lattice spacing of silicon crystals (1987Co39). 2000He14 fitted the    
 75AS4cG revised |g-ray energies to a level scheme. The values given here are   
 75AS5cG their recommended level-energy differences                             
 75AS cG E(P)$From 1977Pr08                                                     
 75AS cG E(R)$From 2005Ra29                                                     
 75AS cG E(D),RI(D)$From Adopted Gammas. This |g ray was reported by            
 75AS2cG 2005Ra29 and 1977Pr08 with an intensity much larger than expected      
 75AS3cG from Adopted Gammas, where the branching ratio is taken from           
 75AS4cG Coulomb excitation which populates 822 level strongly. The evaluators  
 75AS5cG thus consider the observation of this |g ray in 2005Ra29 and           
 75AS6cG 1977Pr08 as suspect                                                    
 75AS cG M$From measured conversion coefficients determined by evaluators       
 75AS2cG from relative conversion electron and photon intensities, using        
 75AS2cG |a(K)(121|g)=0.0372 and |a(K)(136|g)=0.0263 theoretical values (from   
 75AS3cG BrIcc) for E1 multipolarity to normalize scales for the electron and   
 75AS4cG photon intensities. The electron intensities used were weighted        
 75AS5cG averages (LWM) from 1955Sc09, 1959Me76, 1960De06, 1960Gr03, and        
 75AS6cG 1961Ed02. Intensities from 2005Ra29 were not included due to many      
 75AS7cG inconsistencies in this paper. Only in a few cases their |a(K)exp      
 75ASxcG values have been used                                                  
 75AS cL E$Deduced from a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies.                 
 75AS cL J,T$From Adopted Levels, unless otherwise stated                       
